Third-party material

The per-file list (author, source, license) is in ATTRIBUTION.md.

Inter font (assets/fonts/Inter-*.ttf): SIL Open Font License 1.1. See assets/fonts/OFL-Inter.txt.
JetBrains Mono font (assets/fonts/JetBrainsMono-Regular.ttf): SIL Open Font License 1.1. See
assets/fonts/OFL-JetBrainsMono.txt. Both are embedded in the desktop binary.

The desktop binary also still embeds egui's default fonts as fallbacks, through the
`epaint_default_fonts` crate (Ubuntu-Light under the Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0, Hack under MIT,
Noto Emoji under OFL-1.1, emoji-icon-font under MIT); their licences ship with that crate.

Sibling-app crates used as dependencies (git, pinned by commit; MIT OR Apache-2.0; not copied):
- photocraft-psd (storytold/photocraft crates/psd, rev c699e3cda69f4852b43c0b191ab0091aaeff9d6a, release 0.9.0):
  PSD/PSB composite for thumbnails (crates/thumbs/src/decoders/psd.rs).
- lightcraft-raw, lightcraft-meta and their lightcraft-tiff/-geom/-color/-raster dependencies
  (storytold/lightcraft, rev 16dbb90499d3c63a6582fcbba1b2550a6e2da032, release 0.8.0): camera raw embedded
  previews and orientation (crates/thumbs/src/decoders/raw.rs).
- lightcraft-heif (same repository and rev) over heic-rs 0.1.4 (MIT OR Apache-2.0): HEIF/HEIC
  thumbnails (crates/thumbs/src/decoders/heif.rs), compiled in only with the opt-in `heic` cargo
  feature (off by default; `cargo build -p assetcraft --features heic`) and then used only after
  the user turns on View > Formats > HEIC. Default builds contain neither crate. HEVC may be
  patent-encumbered in some countries.

